		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4400&amp;p=34380#p34380"><![CDATA[
Thank you for the explanations, very helpful -<br><br>I already stumbled across this line when I was inspecting the display code <div class="codebox"><p>CODE: </p><pre><code>*((volatile uint8_t*) LCD_FSMC_ADDR_DATA) = 0;// write 0 to the display pins , to pull them all low, so keyboard reads don't need to</code></pre></div>And I fully agree that setting the pins to output again - do nothing - and resetting them back to input should not really have an effect. <br><br>But I tested my device now for several hours and used the keypad and buttons intensively. It works perfectly.<br><br>I zipped and attached the files below. <br>Maybe you can manage to create a build and test with the device of your friend you mentioned in another post above. <br>It would be interesting to see if it also works for his device. <br><br><br>Recarding the CPU .<br><br>CPU : "STM"<br>CPU Sig: 0x0413<br>CPU Rev: 0x1007<br>CPU Pack: 0x0005<dl class="file"><dt><span class="imageset icon_topic_attach"></span> <a class="postlink" href="http://localhost/opengd77/download/file.php?id=2755&amp;sid=f2ea866ab1ac0cf5e20c22bca363464e">mod.zip</a></dt></dl><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=7411">hb9gnb</a> — Thu Dec 05, 2024 6:42 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
