Not reading key "0" just leads to other keys emitting events....<br><br>I have changed the readKeys to <br><div class="codebox"><p>CODE: </p><pre><code>uint32_t keyboardRead(void){uint32_t result = KEY_NONE;GPIO_InitTypeDef GPIO_InitStruct = { 0 };GPIO_InitStruct.Mode = GPIO_MODE_OUTPUT_PP;    &lt;---------------  outputGPIO_InitStruct.Speed = GPIO_SPEED_FREQ_LOW;GPIO_InitStruct.Pull = GPIO_PULLDOWN;GPIO_InitStruct.Pin = LCD_D0_Pin | LCD_D1_Pin | LCD_D2_Pin | LCD_D3_Pin;HAL_GPIO_Init(GPIOD, &amp;GPIO_InitStruct);GPIO_InitStruct.Pin = LCD_D4_Pin | LCD_D5_Pin | LCD_D6_Pin | LCD_D7_Pin;HAL_GPIO_Init(GPIOE, &amp;GPIO_InitStruct);GPIO_InitStruct.Mode = GPIO_MODE_INPUT;   &lt;--------------- back to inputGPIO_InitStruct.Pin = LCD_D0_Pin | LCD_D1_Pin | LCD_D2_Pin | LCD_D3_Pin;HAL_GPIO_Init(GPIOD, &amp;GPIO_InitStruct);GPIO_InitStruct.Pin = LCD_D4_Pin | LCD_D5_Pin | LCD_D6_Pin | LCD_D7_Pin;HAL_GPIO_Init(GPIOE, &amp;GPIO_InitStruct);and also in buttons.c{GPIO_InitTypeDef GPIO_InitStruct = {0};uint32_t result = BUTTON_NONE;GPIO_InitStruct.Mode = GPIO_MODE_OUTPUT_PP;   &lt;-------------- outputGPIO_InitStruct.Speed = GPIO_SPEED_FREQ_LOW;GPIO_InitStruct.Pull = GPIO_PULLDOWN;GPIO_InitStruct.Pin =#if defined(PLATFORM_RT84_DM1701) || defined(PLATFORM_MD2017)LCD_D5_Pin |#endif#if ! defined(PLATFORM_MD2017)LCD_D6_Pin |#endifLCD_D7_Pin;HAL_GPIO_Init(GPIOE, &amp;GPIO_InitStruct);GPIO_InitStruct.Mode = GPIO_MODE_INPUT;   &lt;---- inputHAL_GPIO_Init(GPIOE, &amp;GPIO_InitStruct);</code></pre></div><br><br><br>This seems to work for me... at least until now... will test it a bit longer to be sure....<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=7411">hb9gnb</a> — Wed Dec 04, 2024 8:05 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
