OK<br><br>-&gt;  Are you a professional programmer??<br>I am working as a software engineer with a master degree in computer science for a rail company. Working mainly with Backend Services. <br>But I do not work with embedded systems. All my knowledge I have with embedded systems is from my education in the module "linux kernel development in RT System with Xenomai " where we programmed a few linux kernel modules with some interrupt handlers for real time embedded devices. So I know what a Chip Select a pullup or a pulldown is. But again not working in this area in my daily life. <br><br><br>To the suggestions <br><br>I tried with PULLUP and PULLDOWN instead of  GPIO_InitStruct.Pull = GPIO_NOPULL <br>result -&gt; keypad is not working at all. <br><br>changing the PortSpeed does not have any effect. <br><br>I also changed the code that it reads the pin 3 times and waits between each read. But this did also have no effect. <br>Works still in the same way. <br><br>In my device it is always Key "0" that is emitted as KEY_EVENT. this evening I will invest more time and try to not read that "0" key at all. <br>just to see if there are other keys causing problems, or if it is just related to this row and gpio pin for key "0"<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=7411">hb9gnb</a> — Wed Dec 04, 2024 10:39 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
