I saw the same problem back in the early days of the development. <br><br>The settling delay is needed and was added to allow for the capacitance and pull up resistors of the keyboard matrix. It takes a noticeable time for the signals on the selected and unselected rows to stabilise to the correct levels. So reading them too early can result in ghost key presses like you are seeing.  There will be differences between individual radios so the current delay might be on the edge of working for your radio.  It could be that small changes in temperature or humidity are causing the settling time to vary. <br><br>Those delays are quite short so there is probably no harm in doubling them for everybody. <br><br>Colin G4EML<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=87">G4EML</a> — Tue Dec 03, 2024 11:41 am</p><hr />
